^CONVERSION ERROR$
unexpected expression: struct_tag
found no match for symbol 'swap'
\* identifier: std::tag-__not_<
--
Per [temp.deduct]/7-8 substitution failures during the deduction
process (including default-template-argument substitution) are
silently absorbed during overload resolution: no diagnostic is
emitted and the failing candidate is simply discarded.

This test was previously KNOWNBUG because CBMC leaked
`unexpected expression: struct_tag` + `irep::pretty()` dump + a
cascading `found no match for symbol 'swap'` when processing
libstdc++'s `std::is_swappable<T>` via `swap(_Tp&, _Tp&)` whose
return type is `_Require<__not_<__is_tuple_like<_Tp>>, ...>`.

Fixed by two null-message-handler wraps per [temp.deduct]/7-8:
 * Around `guess_function_template_args(old_id, fargs)` in
   `cpp_typecheck_resolve.cpp` (per-candidate substitution).
 * Around `typecheck_type(arg.type())` for default TYPE template
   arguments in `cpp_typecheck_template.cpp` (i >= first_default).

`static_assert(std::is_swappable<double>::value)` now evaluates to
true with no user-visible diagnostic.  The minimum-reproducer
distilled from a user harness that transitively includes <array>,
which in turn instantiates
`std::array<double, N>` -> `std::__array_traits<double, N>` ->
`std::__is_swappable<double>` -> `std::__is_swappable_impl<double>`.
